# Plan 08-16 (D-18): runner-process.roundtrip.<id>, the scenario run with ivs-run --roundtrip-at-ticks <n> (a save, a power-on reset and a restore at every
#   multiple of n) must give the plain report apart from host.calls and must have cut (host.calls grows by two per cut): five scenarios, diag-boot-pass,
#   diag-ctrl-psg-pass, diag-stic-fgbg-pass, demo-lamp-tone-pass and diag-stic2-collision-pass (the process-level witness of the MOB, border, delay and
#   collision state), each with a value derived by arithmetic from its run length (see tests/runner-process-tap.sh);
#   runner-process.roundtrip.refuse-range: zero, one above the maximum, a missing value and a repeated option are each exit 14 with the message line and the usage
#   text on stderr and no report; runner-process.judge.roundtrip-differs: the comparison fails on a report of another scenario (body-differs) and on a hook run
#   that did not cut (roundtrip-no-cut).
